utput': 'Evaluation: You hold Two Pair (Queens and Fours) on a board of 4s, 7d, Qd, 6d. While your hand is strong, the board is very "wet" (dangerous). The 6 of Diamonds on the turn places a third diamond on the board, completing potential flushes, and also connects straight draws (any 5 makes a straight). Since the opponent called your flop bet, they likely have a piece of the board or a draw that may have just improved.\n\nReason: Checking is the best move for pot control. It prevents you from building a large pot in a situation where you could be drawing dead against a flush or straight. It allows you to see what the opponent does; if they check, you see a river for free. If they bet, you can re-evaluate based on the bet size, rather than opening yourself up to a check-raise.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
